  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAt base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`, the historical parity-side audit spends most time in `scripts/binary_phase_frames.py`: `basis` and `contains` are called millions of times, and `contains` previously rebuilt `basis(space)` twice per membership test.\n\nThis PR memoizes `basis` on the row tuple and implements `contains` by reducing the vector against one basis of the space. The highest-bit pivot rule, elimination order, classify/nullspace/residual APIs and every Boolean result are unchanged. Only the source pin for `scripts/binary_phase_frames.py` changes inside the three certificates that bind that file (`parity-side`, `disjoint-tensor-compression`, `dyadic-central-factor`).\n\n**Tooling improvement; no new kappa.** Selected frontier untouched.\n\n## Result\n\nOn Linux / CPython 3.12.3, five alternating fresh-process pairs of the full `h=8,10,26` stream gave median **27.349 \u2192 13.463 s (2.03\u00d7)**. Timing is host-descriptive and is not a correctness gate. Every experiment receipt matches the baseline checker fieldwise.\n\nPackage: `research/parity-side-basis-cache/`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/parity-side-basis-cache/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/parity-side-basis-cache/verify.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/parity-side-basis-cache\npython3.12 -I -B research/parity-side-basis-cache/benchmark.py --rounds 5\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_PARITY_SIDE_BASIS_CACHE h=[8, 10, 26] roles=[724, 2271, 82720] repaired=[938, 3283, 308336] ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/parity-side-basis-cache outcome=completed\nPASS_IDENTICAL_PARITY_SIDE_RECEIPTS\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Full `make verify`, selected cold replay, Lean, and multiplication-theorem obligations were not rerun for this isolated historical-checker change.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest priors (different objects): [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#756](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/756), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1793](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1793), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1217](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1217). No competing open PR on this object at refresh.\n\nDouglas R. Colkitt authored the parity-side obstruction, repair and original binary phase-frame checkers. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
